        "id": 1494168536,
        "content": "This is only used for meta purposes. For example, for our team to be financially incentivized to work on this repo we can config the settings of the bot's behavior on our org's instance. \r\nI'm just saying that in the actual package distribution this is not necessary. \r\nThe bot will automatically inherit the organization config (`@ubiquibot/ubiquibot-config/.github/ubiquibot-config.yml`) and if neither the repo or org config exists, then yes there are some built in defaults (which basically disable the bot from doing anything intrusive, for new partners to get started easily.)",
